{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778695655,"nonce":"53mzQPAzHKAgrx5k0lhVEyvfyqA=","title":"Package Mandible channel server as a plugin and submit to Anthropic's official marketplace","message":"Mandible's MCP channel server (currently in `channel-server/`) needs to be packaged as a Claude Code plugin and submitted to the official Anthropic marketplace so that personal-account users can register it without `--dangerously-load-development-channels`.\n\n## Why\n\nThe current `cx` wrapper invokes:\n\n```\nclaude --dangerously-load-development-channels --channels server:mandible ...\n```\n\nClaude Code 2.1.140+ rejects `--channels server:mandible` without the `--dangerously-load-development-channels` flag. Per the channels-reference docs (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/channels-reference):\n\n\u003e `server:` entries (bare `.mcp.json` server names) always require `--dangerously-load-development-channels`. The approved allowlist (`allowedChannelPlugins`) accepts only `plugin:` entries, and is Team/Enterprise managed-settings only.\n\nThis means every Claude Code startup currently presents a confirmation dialog (\"WARNING: Loading development channels\"). There is no personal-account workaround. The only way to suppress the dialog without compromising on functionality is to publish the Mandible channel as a plugin on the Anthropic-curated marketplace (`claude-plugins-official`).\n\n## Requirements\n\n1. **Wrap `channel-server/` as a Claude Code plugin.** Add a `plugin.json` and any marketplace metadata required by `code.claude.com/docs/en/channels-reference` (\"Package as a plugin\" section). The plugin should expose the same MCP server entry-point already in use.\n2. **Publish under a marketplace.** Initially this can be a local or self-hosted marketplace for validation; later, submit to `claude-plugins-official`.\n3. **Submit to `claude-plugins-official` for security review.** Anthropic curates the official marketplace; submission process is documented in the channels-reference docs.\n\n## Until approved\n\n`--channels plugin:mandible@\u003cmarketplace\u003e` still requires `--dangerously-load-development-channels` per the docs while the plugin is unapproved. The current best workaround is to revert `cx` to the pre-May-11 invocation (`--dangerously-load-development-channels server:mandible`) — the startup dialog stays but at least the channel works. The revert is being submitted as a separate dotfiles change against issue `9c8daf7`.\n\n## Cross-refs\n\n- dotfiles `9c8daf7` (channel-server wiring; the bad swap commit `07071f5` is being reverted there)\n- Channels reference docs: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/channels-reference","files":null}]}